{"abstract":[{"text":"Start and stop servers, and know which code runs on which thread.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/ThreadingAndLifecycle"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"NanoHTTP"}],"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Threading and Lifecycle"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"anchor":"Starting-and-stopping","level":3,"text":"Starting and stopping","type":"heading"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","server.get[\"/ping\"] = { _ in .ok(.text(\"pong\")) }","try server.start(0)                         // port 0: any free port","let port = try server.port()","print(\"listening at port \\(port), state: \\(server.state)\")      // .running","server.stop()                                                   // .stopped","try server.start(UInt16(port))                                 // a stopped server can be started again","server.stop()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/start(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns as soon as the server listens, and throws if the socket cannot be set up:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the port is in use, or the listen address is not an address of this machine","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/listenAddress","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). The server is stopped then. Starting a server that is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stopped does nothing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/stop()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" closes the listening socket and all open connections, and returns when that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"done. Connections that are in the middle of a response fail to write it. Stopping a server that is not running","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does nothing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both can be called from any thread, also at the same time: exactly one call does the work.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/state-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"starting","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"running","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"stopping","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"stopped","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/operating","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"true while it is running; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/openConnections","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" counts the open connections.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A server starts with its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/configuration-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; changing it while the server runs takes effect the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"next time it is started.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Which-thread-runs-what","level":3,"text":"Which thread runs what","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"accept loop","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" runs on one thread of its own (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/acceptQoS","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".userInitiated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by default).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every accepted connection is served by a thread of its own (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/connectionQoS","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".userInitiated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by default), not by a thread of the dispatch queues, which could not hold many blocked threads.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The threads are reused: a thread that has finished its connection waits for the next one for a few seconds.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The thread reads a request, calls the middleware and the handler, writes the response, and reads the next","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. It is blocked in the read while the connection waits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Connections are therefore served ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"concurrently","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", and the requests of one connection one after another.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Handlers, middleware and the closures of WebSocket sessions run on these threads: anything they share has to be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protected. (Or run the server on one thread, see below.)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"code":["// file scope","final class ExampleCounter {","  private let lock = NSLock()","  private var value = 0","","  func next() -> Int {","    lock.lock()","    defer { lock.unlock() }","    value += 1","    return value","  }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"code":["let counter = ExampleCounter()","let server = NanoHTTPServer()","server.get[\"/visits\"] = { _ in .ok(.text(\"visit \\(counter.next())\")) }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Routes can be registered while the server runs. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer/middleware","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer/notFoundHandler","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" are plain properties: set them up before starting.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Running-everything-on-one-thread","level":3,"text":"Running everything on one thread","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A server can do all its work on a single thread: accepting connections, reading requests, the middleware, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handlers, writing responses. Requests are then served one at a time, and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"handlers need no locks","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","server.configuration.threading = .singleThread","var visits = 0                          // shared by all handlers, and needs no lock","server.get[\"/visits\"] = { _ in","  visits += 1","  return .ok(.text(\"visit \\(visits)\"))","}","try server.run(8080)                    // serves on this thread until the server is stopped"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/run(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" serves on the calling thread, which returns when the server is stopped (from a signal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler or another thread). ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/start(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns at once and uses one thread of its own instead; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handlers run on it, never on the thread that called ","type":"text"},{"code":"start","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The thread waits for all connections together, so connections that wait for a request cost nothing and block no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one: a browser that opens a few connections it does not use, or keeps them alive, does not slow the server down.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"What blocks the thread does block the server:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A slow handler delays every other request.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A request that stalls half way delays the others for up to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"readTimeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a client that does not read its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"response for up to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"writeTimeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (30 seconds each by default): lower them for a server like this.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The messages of WebSockets are handled by the one thread as well, one at a time between other work: a closure that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes long delays everything, and a message that stalls half way delays the server up to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"readTimeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". See","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/WebSockets#On-a-server-with-one-thread","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","server.configuration.threading = .singleThread","server.configuration.readTimeout = 5","server.configuration.writeTimeout = 5"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The threading mode is part of the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/configuration-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and changing it takes effect when the server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is started the next time. With threads per connection, ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accepts connections on the calling thread and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connections still have threads of their own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Idle-connections-timeouts-and-the-number-of-connections","level":3,"text":"Idle connections, timeouts and the number of connections","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every connection occupies a thread and a file descriptor for as long as it is open, so the server limits both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"what a connection may waste and how many there are (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Setting","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Default","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What happens","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"idleTimeout","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"60 s","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A connection that sends nothing, as its first request or between two requests (connections are persistent), is closed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"readTimeout","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"30 s","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A request that has begun but stalls for this long is answered with ","type":"text"},{"code":"408 Request Timeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"writeTimeout","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"30 s","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A connection whose peer takes no data for this long is closed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"maxConnections","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"128","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A connection that arrives when that many are open is answered with ","type":"text"},{"code":"503 Service Unavailable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" turns a limit off. (On a server that runs on one thread the idle connections cost no thread, but they still count.) The timeouts are pauses, not total times: a large upload that keeps arriving is not cut","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"off, and a handler may take as long as it likes. WebSocket sessions are not subject to the idle and read timeouts,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but they count as connections.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","server.configuration.idleTimeout = 10        // drop silent connections sooner","server.configuration.maxConnections = 32     // a small embedded server"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Accepting-under-pressure","level":3,"text":"Accepting under pressure","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the process runs out of file descriptors, accepting is paused for a moment (and logged) instead of stopping the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"server, and goes on when descriptors are free again. Connections that arrive during such a shortage can be lost.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Reacting-to-termination","level":3,"text":"Reacting to termination","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A command-line tool can stop the server when it is terminated (Ctrl-C, ","type":"text"},{"code":"kill","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", closing the terminal).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoProcess/watchSignals(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" calls a function when the process receives ","type":"text"},{"code":"SIGINT","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SIGTERM","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"SIGHUP","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The function","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"runs on a queue of its own, not inside the signal handler, so it may do what it needs to: stopping the server makes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/run(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" return, and the program ends normally.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","NanoProcess.watchSignals { _ in","  server.stop()","}","try server.run(8080)","print(\"The server has stopped.\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Once the process watches these signals, it no longer ends by itself when it receives one: the function has to see to that.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(A program that does not return from ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can call ","type":"text"},{"code":"exit(0)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the function instead.)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP":{"abstract":[{"text":"A small HTTP/1.1 server for apps and tools: routing, files, forms, uploads and WebSockets, without dependencies.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"NanoHTTP","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/HowARequestIsServed":{"abstract":[{"text":"Follow a request from the socket to your handler and back.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/HowARequestIsServed","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"How a Request Is Served","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/howarequestisserved"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/Logging":{"abstract":[{"text":"See what the server reports, and send it where you want it.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/Logging","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Logging","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/logging"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/MiddlewareAndExtending":{"abstract":[{"text":"Look at every request before it is routed, and replace parts of the server by subclassing.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/MiddlewareAndExtending","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Middleware and Extending the Server","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/middlewareandextending"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoConsoleLogger":{"abstract":[{"text":"A logger that prints one line for every message, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[WARNING] Unable to accept a connection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for command-line tools and for tests. By default the lines are printed to the standard output, and every line is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flushed: when the output goes to a pipe or a file (","type":"text"},{"code":"tool | tee log","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), the standard output is buffered, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lines would otherwise show up late.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoConsoleLogger"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoConsoleLogger","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoConsoleLogger"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoConsoleLogger","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanoconsolelogger"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPConnection":{"abstract":[{"text":"A request that has been read from a connection, together with the handler that will answer it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/handle(connection:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" drives the connection with it: ","type":"text"},{"code":"send(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"response and returns the connection for the next request, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the connection has ended.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPConnection"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPConnection","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPConnection"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPConnection","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpconnection"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPDeferredResponse":{"abstract":[{"text":"The answer to a request that is sent later, from any thread.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPDeferredResponse"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPDeferredResponse","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPDeferredResponse"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPDeferredResponse","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpdeferredresponse"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPLogger":{"abstract":[{"text":"Receives the messages that a server reports: a response that could not be written, a pause in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepting connections, a handler that threw an error, a WebSocket client that broke the protocol.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Set the logger of a server with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/logger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPLogger"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPLogger","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPLogger"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPLogger","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttplogger"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer":{"abstract":[{"text":"An HTTP/1.1 server with routing.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServer"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServer"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPServer","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserver"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer/middleware":{"abstract":[{"text":"Functions that wrap the handling of every request, in the order of the array: the first one is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"outermost. A middleware receives the request and ","type":"text"},{"code":"next","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the rest of the chain: the middleware after it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and finally the router and the handler. It lets the request through by calling ","type":"text"},{"code":"next","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and can","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"middleware"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A14HTTPMiddlewarea","text":"NanoHTTPMiddleware"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer/middleware","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"middleware","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserver/middleware"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer/notFoundHandler":{"abstract":[{"text":"The handler for requests that no route matches. Without one, such requests are answered with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"404 Not Found","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and an empty body.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"notFoundHandler"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A18HTTPRequestHandlera","text":"NanoHTTPRequestHandler"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer/notFoundHandler","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"notFoundHandler","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserver/notfoundhandler"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO":{"abstract":[{"text":"The part of a server that deals with sockets and threads: it listens at a port, accepts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connections, reads the requests of each connection on a thread of its own, hands them to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/dispatch(request:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and writes the responses. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" builds routing on top of it;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subclass this class to use the server without routing.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServerIO"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServerIO"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPServerIO","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"text":"How a server listens and what it accepts. Change it before ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/start(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"running server keeps the configuration it was started with.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Configuration"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Configuration"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPServerIO.Configuration","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/acceptQoS":{"abstract":[{"text":"The priority of the thread that accepts connections.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"acceptQoS"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@E@NSQualityOfService","text":"QualityOfService"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/acceptQoS","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"acceptQoS","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/acceptqos"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/connectionQoS":{"abstract":[{"text":"The priority of the threads that serve the connections.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"connectionQoS"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@E@NSQualityOfService","text":"QualityOfService"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/connectionQoS","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"connectionQoS","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/connectionqos"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/listenAddress":{"abstract":[{"text":"Where the server listens. The default is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/NanoListenAddress/loopback","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": only programs on this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"machine can connect. Use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/NanoListenAddress/allInterfaces","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a server that is meant to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be reached from other devices.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"listenAddress"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A12HTTPServerIOC0A13ListenAddressO","text":"NanoListenAddress"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/listenAddress","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"listenAddress","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/listenaddress"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/logger":{"abstract":[{"text":"Receives what the server reports: a response that could not be written, a pause in accepting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connections, a handler that threw an error, a WebSocket client that broke the protocol. The default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoOSLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which writes to the unified logging system (the console of Xcode, the Console","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app). A command-line tool that should print to its terminal uses a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoConsoleLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoSilentLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" switches logging off.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"logger"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentif